data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — openzeppelin-contracts@5.7.0\n_human-validated 2026-08-19 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/openzeppelin-contracts/erc20-transfer-hook.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-19, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test, fork\n- chains exercised: none\n- on-chain:\n  - none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.\n- gas: see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition.\n\n# Recipe: openzeppelin-contracts @5 :: erc20-transfer-hook\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-19 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 12 quotes · 10 structural · 7 forge assertions, on a local EVM, no chain and no key. The four gas figures came back BYTE-IDENTICAL to the author run on a different machine — these are deterministic, unlike #15's fork figures, and that is measured rather than assumed.\nproject_id: \"openzeppelin-contracts\"   # the corpus id, as artifacts/p1-projects-v1.json has it\nversion_major: 5                       # §2's ordinary meaning: a real semver major of one package\nversion: \"5.7.0\"                       # ⚠ THE TAG ACTUALLY RUN — resolved to commit\n                                       #   cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3 and recorded\n                                       #   in foundry.lock by `forge install`. NOT npm's `latest`,\n                                       #   which on 2026-08-19 was 5.6.1 — see mistake #5.\ntype: \"erc20-transfer-hook\"\n\n# ⚠ NO CHAIN IS EXERCISED, AND THE EMPTY LIST IS THE HONEST VALUE (SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §4).\n# This is a LIBRARY recipe: the suite compiles the pinned tag and runs it on a local EVM. There\n# is no fork, no RPC, no key and no funds. Every other recipe in this repo touches a chain, so\n# the temptation is to write `[ethereum]` because the code is obviously usable there — that\n# would be claiming an exercise nobody performed. This row is the first with `chains: []`.\nchains: []\n\n# ── DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndeployments: {}\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"openzeppelin-contracts\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── TransferFeeToken.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    import {ERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\n\n    /// Custom logic on EVERY movement of an OpenZeppelin Contracts v5 ERC-20.\n    ///\n    /// v5 has ONE hook: `_update(from, to, value)`. It carries transfers, mints and burns alike —\n    /// a mint arrives as `from == address(0)`, a burn as `to == address(0)`.\n    ///\n    /// ⚠ `_beforeTokenTransfer` and `_afterTokenTransfer` belong to OpenZeppelin Contracts 4.9.6.\n    ///   They were DELETED in 5.0.0 and do not exist at the 5.7.0 this is compiled against. If you\n    ///   are porting OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 code: the body of `_beforeTokenTransfer` goes ABOVE\n    ///   `super._update`, and the body of `_afterTokenTransfer` goes BELOW it.\n    contract TransferFeeToken is ERC20 {\n        /// 1% of every ordinary transfer, in basis points.\n        uint16 public constant FEE_BPS = 100;\n\n        address public immutable treasury;\n\n        // Counters, so the hook's reach is observable rather than asserted.\n        uint256 public transfersSeen;\n        uint256 public mintsSeen;\n        uint256 public burnsSeen;\n\n        /// Written AFTER super._update — the OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 `_afterTokenTransfer` position,\n        /// where balances have already moved.\n        uint256 public recipientBalanceAfterLastTransfer;\n\n        constructor(address treasury_) ERC20(\"Transfer Fee Token\", \"TFT\") {\n            treasury = treasury_;\n        }\n\n        function mint(address to, uint256 value) external {\n            _mint(to, value);\n        }\n\n        function burn(uint256 value) external {\n            _burn(msg.sender, value);\n        }\n\n        /// The single v5 hook. Every balance change in this token passes through here.\n        function _update(address from, address to, uint256 value) internal override {\n            // ⚠ MINTS AND BURNS COME THROUGH HERE TOO, with address(0) on one side. Without this\n            //   guard the fee below is charged on both: measured, a naive 1% fee diverts 1% of\n            //   every mint to the treasury and destroys only 99 of every 100 tokens burned.\n            if (from == address(0) || to == address(0)) {\n                if (from == address(0)) mintsSeen++;\n                else burnsSeen++;\n                super._update(from, to, value);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            // ── the OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 `_beforeTokenTransfer` position: balances have NOT moved ──\n            transfersSeen++;\n\n            uint256 fee = (value * FEE_BPS) / 10_000;\n            if (fee > 0) {\n                // ⚠ TWO super._update CALLS, NOT `_transfer`. `_transfer` is not virtual in v5 and\n                //   it calls `_update`, so invoking it from here re-enters this function until the\n                //   call runs out of gas. Split the amount and move each part with super instead.\n                super._update(from, treasury, fee);\n            }\n            super._update(from, to, value - fee);\n\n            // ── the OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 `_afterTokenTransfer` position: balances HAVE moved ──\n            recipientBalanceAfterLastTransfer = balanceOf(to);\n        }\n    }\n\n# ── INTERFACE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninterface:\n  lang: \"solidity\"\n  body: |\n    // OpenZeppelin Contracts v5.7.0 — the ERC20 internals a transfer hook actually touches.\n    // Everything marked OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 below is REAL, and real at a version this is not.\n\n    abstract contract ERC20 /* is Context, IERC20, IERC20Metadata, IERC20Errors */ {\n        // ⭐ THE HOOK. The single extension point in v5, and it carries every balance change:\n        //    a transfer (both non-zero), a MINT (from == address(0)) and a BURN (to == address(0)).\n        //    An override MUST call super._update or nothing moves — silently.\n        function _update(address from, address to, uint256 value) internal virtual;\n\n        // ⚠ NOT virtual in v5. You cannot override these; the compiler refuses with\n        //   \"Trying to override non-virtual function.\" Overriding _update is not the preferred\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 39104 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:openzeppelin-contracts@5.7.0::erc20-transfer-hook::body@6040\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\n- https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/CHANGELOG.md\n- https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/tree/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3\n- https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/tree/dc44c9f1a4c3b10af99492eed84f83ed244203f6\n\n---\n\n### openzeppelin-contracts@5.x::BridgeERC20::__contract__\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/contracts/crosschain/bridges/BridgeERC20.sol#L19-L42\n\n```\nabstract contract BridgeERC20 is BridgeFungible {\n    using SafeERC20 for IERC20;\n```\n\n### 132c5b42-d4e0-5b7f-9faf-96812c7ad72d\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L20-L20\n\n```\n<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › Overview\n```\n\n### 7a5f1eaa-c990-5118-9746-7ea5fa7f4220\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L32-L32\n\n```\n<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › Overview › Installation\n```\n\n### 1832d834-8435-5338-8a08-c7933a4deffe\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L115-L117\n\n```\n<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › License\nOpenZeppelin Contracts is released under the [MIT License](LICENSE).\n```\n\n### 291871e5-56c0-522a-bb6f-1c27e7cbc01e\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L119-L121\n\n```\n<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › Legal\nYour use of this Project is governed by the terms found at www.openzeppelin.com/tos (the \"Terms\").\n```\n\n### 11b9734e-4084-556d-aa8c-db9c5f8313f0\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L34-L44\n\n```\n<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › Overview › Installation › Hardhat (npm)\n```\n$ npm install @openzeppelin/contracts\n```\n→ Installs the latest audited release (`latest`).\n\n```\n$ npm install @openzeppelin/contracts@dev\n```\n→ Installs the latest unaudited release (`dev`).\n```\n\n### 173d12c0-4f59-5c2e-9488-97ad13f1153e\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L111-L113\n\n```\n<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › Contribute\nOpenZeppelin Contracts exists thanks to its contributors. There are many ways you can participate and help build high quality software. Check out the [contribution guide](CONTRIBUTING.md)!\n```\n\n### openzeppelin-contracts@5.x::ERC1363ReturnFalseOnERC20Mock::__contract__\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/contracts/mocks/token/ERC1363ReturnFalseMock.sol#L8-L20\n\n```\nabstract contract ERC1363ReturnFalseOnERC20Mock is ERC1363 {\n    function transfer(address, uint256) public pure override(IERC20, ERC20) returns (bool) {\n```\n\n### openzeppelin-contracts@5.x::SafeERC20::SafeERC20FailedOperation\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol#L20-L55\n\n```\nerror SafeERC20FailedOperation(address token);\nerror SafeERC20FailedDecreaseAllowance(address spender, uint256 currentAllowance, uint256 requestedDecrease);\nfunction safeTransfer(IERC20 token, address to, uint256 value) internal\n+2 more units in this chunk\n```\n\n### 788c4e47-3eff-547e-af61-097592d02c77\n`openzeppelin-contracts@5.x` · repo:bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40 · as_of 2026-08-03T16:17:02Z\nhttps://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/audits/2017-03.md#L1-L6\n\n```\nOpenZeppelin Audit\nNOTE ON 2021-07-19: This report makes reference to Zeppelin, OpenZeppelin, OpenZeppelin Contracts, the OpenZeppelin team, and OpenZeppelin library. Many of these things have since been renamed and know that this audit applies to what is currently called the OpenZeppelin…\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"openzeppelin-contracts","version":"5.7.0","recipe_type":"erc20-transfer-hook","last_validated":"2026-08-19","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-19","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test","fork"],"chains_exercised":[],"on_chain":"none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.","gas":"see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition."},"body":"# Recipe: openzeppelin-contracts @5 :: erc20-transfer-hook\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-19 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 12 quotes · 10 structural · 7 forge assertions, on a local EVM, no chain and no key. The four gas figures came back BYTE-IDENTICAL to the author run on a different machine — these are deterministic, unlike #15's fork figures, and that is measured rather than assumed.\nproject_id: \"openzeppelin-contracts\"   # the corpus id, as artifacts/p1-projects-v1.json has it\nversion_major: 5                       # §2's ordinary meaning: a real semver major of one package\nversion: \"5.7.0\"                       # ⚠ THE TAG ACTUALLY RUN — resolved to commit\n                                       #   cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3 and recorded\n                                       #   in foundry.lock by `forge install`. NOT npm's `latest`,\n                                       #   which on 2026-08-19 was 5.6.1 — see mistake #5.\ntype: \"erc20-transfer-hook\"\n\n# ⚠ NO CHAIN IS EXERCISED, AND THE EMPTY LIST IS THE HONEST VALUE (SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §4).\n# This is a LIBRARY recipe: the suite compiles the pinned tag and runs it on a local EVM. There\n# is no fork, no RPC, no key and no funds. Every other recipe in this repo touches a chain, so\n# the temptation is to write `[ethereum]` because the code is obviously usable there — that\n# would be claiming an exercise nobody performed. This row is the first with `chains: []`.\nchains: []\n\n# ── DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndeployments: {}\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"openzeppelin-contracts\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── TransferFeeToken.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    import {ERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\n\n    /// Custom logic on EVERY movement of an OpenZeppelin Contracts v5 ERC-20.\n    ///\n    /// v5 has ONE hook: `_update(from, to, value)`. It carries transfers, mints and burns alike —\n    /// a mint arrives as `from == address(0)`, a burn as `to == address(0)`.\n    ///\n    /// ⚠ `_beforeTokenTransfer` and `_afterTokenTransfer` belong to OpenZeppelin Contracts 4.9.6.\n    ///   They were DELETED in 5.0.0 and do not exist at the 5.7.0 this is compiled against. If you\n    ///   are porting OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 code: the body of `_beforeTokenTransfer` goes ABOVE\n    ///   `super._update`, and the body of `_afterTokenTransfer` goes BELOW it.\n    contract TransferFeeToken is ERC20 {\n        /// 1% of every ordinary transfer, in basis points.\n        uint16 public constant FEE_BPS = 100;\n\n        address public immutable treasury;\n\n        // Counters, so the hook's reach is observable rather than asserted.\n        uint256 public transfersSeen;\n        uint256 public mintsSeen;\n        uint256 public burnsSeen;\n\n        /// Written AFTER super._update — the OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 `_afterTokenTransfer` position,\n        /// where balances have already moved.\n        uint256 public recipientBalanceAfterLastTransfer;\n\n        constructor(address treasury_) ERC20(\"Transfer Fee Token\", \"TFT\") {\n            treasury = treasury_;\n        }\n\n        function mint(address to, uint256 value) external {\n            _mint(to, value);\n        }\n\n        function burn(uint256 value) external {\n            _burn(msg.sender, value);\n        }\n\n        /// The single v5 hook. Every balance change in this token passes through here.\n        function _update(address from, address to, uint256 value) internal override {\n            // ⚠ MINTS AND BURNS COME THROUGH HERE TOO, with address(0) on one side. Without this\n            //   guard the fee below is charged on both: measured, a naive 1% fee diverts 1% of\n            //   every mint to the treasury and destroys only 99 of every 100 tokens burned.\n            if (from == address(0) || to == address(0)) {\n                if (from == address(0)) mintsSeen++;\n                else burnsSeen++;\n                super._update(from, to, value);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            // ── the OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 `_beforeTokenTransfer` position: balances have NOT moved ──\n            transfersSeen++;\n\n            uint256 fee = (value * FEE_BPS) / 10_000;\n            if (fee > 0) {\n                // ⚠ TWO super._update CALLS, NOT `_transfer`. `_transfer` is not virtual in v5 and\n                //   it calls `_update`, so invoking it from here re-enters this function until the\n                //   call runs out of gas. Split the amount and move each part with super instead.\n                super._update(from, treasury, fee);\n            }\n            super._update(from, to, value - fee);\n\n            // ── the OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 `_afterTokenTransfer` position: balances HAVE moved ──\n            recipientBalanceAfterLastTransfer = balanceOf(to);\n        }\n    }\n\n# ── INTERFACE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninterface:\n  lang: \"solidity\"\n  body: |\n    // OpenZeppelin Contracts v5.7.0 — the ERC20 internals a transfer hook actually touches.\n    // Everything marked OpenZeppelin 4.9.6 below is REAL, and real at a version this is not.\n\n    abstract contract ERC20 /* is Context, IERC20, IERC20Metadata, IERC20Errors */ {\n        // ⭐ THE HOOK. The single extension point in v5, and it carries every balance change:\n        //    a transfer (both non-zero), a MINT (from == address(0)) and a BURN (to == address(0)).\n        //    An override MUST call super._update or nothing moves — silently.\n        function _update(address from, address to, uint256 value) internal virtual;\n\n        // ⚠ NOT virtual in v5. You cannot override these; the compiler refuses with\n        //   \"Trying to override non-virtual function.\" Overriding _update is not the preferred","source_path":"recipes/openzeppelin-contracts/erc20-transfer-hook.yaml","requested_version":null,"exact_version_match":null,"body_truncated":true,"body_bytes":39104,"citations":["https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol","https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3/CHANGELOG.md","https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/tree/cab19933c33c2ad1d4c7a84864a3601dddfd16f3","https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/tree/dc44c9f1a4c3b10af99492eed84f83ed244203f6"],"citations_capped":false,"body_cursor":"recipe:openzeppelin-contracts@5.7.0::erc20-transfer-hook::body@6040"},"hits":[{"selector":"openzeppelin-contracts@5.x::BridgeERC20::__contract__","source_url":"https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/contracts/crosschain/bridges/BridgeERC20.sol#L19-L42","snippet":"abstract contract BridgeERC20 is BridgeFungible {\n    using SafeERC20 for IERC20;","project":"openzeppelin-contracts","version":"5.x","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-13T03:54:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T16:17:02Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40"},{"selector":"132c5b42-d4e0-5b7f-9faf-96812c7ad72d","source_url":"https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L20-L20","snippet":"<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › Overview","project":"openzeppelin-contracts","version":"5.x","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-13T03:54:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T16:17:02Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40"},{"selector":"7a5f1eaa-c990-5118-9746-7ea5fa7f4220","source_url":"https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L32-L32","snippet":"<img src=\"logo.svg\" alt=\"OpenZeppelin\" height=\"40px\"> › Overview › Installation","project":"openzeppelin-contracts","version":"5.x","version_defaulted":false,"last_validated":"2026-08-13T03:54:35Z","as_of":"2026-08-03T16:17:02Z","provenance_kind":"repo","pin_ref":"bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40"},{"selector":"1832d834-8435-5338-8a08-c7933a4deffe","source_url":"https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/bb8ed388b04690b09f8c36586f5cde9fdd67fb40/README.md#L115-L117","sn